My point is, users should still be able to define a period in case `IIndicatorWarmUpPeriodProvider.WarmUpPeriod` is not defined. The solution then could be as follows: 

```C#
public void IndicatorBatchUpdate(Symbol symbol, IEnumerable<IIndicator> indicators, Resolution resolution, int period = 0)
{
	if (period == 0)
	{
		period = indicators.Select(indicator => (indicator as IIndicatorWarmUpPeriodProvider)?.WarmUpPeriod ?? 0).Max();
	}

// From here continue as before.

```
